# kino_ash demo — render an Ash surface

A minimal Livebook demo: define a test-style Ash resource with an `a2ui`
block, seed a couple of records, and render the surface with
`KinoAsh.render/2`.

## Dependency setup

Installs `kino_ash` from GitHub. `ash_a2ui` comes in transitively, pinned
inside the package to the exact tree the vendored client hook and
committed bundle were verified against.

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:kino_ash, github: "lukegalea/kino_ash"}
])
```

## Define the demo resource

The smallest possible surface: one table of names. (Apps set Ash's
string-length config in config.exs; a notebook sets it directly before
defining resources.)

```elixir
Application.put_env(:ash, :default_string_length_count, :codepoints)

defmodule Demo.Domain do
  use Ash.Domain, validate_config_inclusion?: false

  resources do
    resource Demo.Minimal
  end
end

defmodule Demo.Minimal do
  use Ash.Resource,
    domain: Demo.Domain,
    data_layer: Ash.DataLayer.Ets,
    extensions: [AshA2ui]

  ets do
    private? true
  end

  attributes do
    uuid_primary_key :id

    attribute :name, :string, public?: true
  end

  actions do
    defaults [:read, :destroy, create: :*, update: :*]
  end

  a2ui do
    component :table do
      fields [:name]
    end
  end
end
```

## Seed some records

```elixir
{:ok, _} = Ash.create(Demo.Minimal, %{name: "Ada Lovelace"})
{:ok, _} = Ash.create(Demo.Minimal, %{name: "Grace Hopper"})
{:ok, _} = Ash.create(Demo.Minimal, %{name: "Alan Turing"})
:ok
```

## Render the surface

The output is a static kino hosting a real `<a2ui-surface>` (the
`@a2ui/lit` web components), hydrated from the encoded messages
`AshA2ui.Info.build_surface/2` produced. Saving the notebook persists a
spec digest — surface id, version, component count — never record data.

```elixir
KinoAsh.render(Demo.Minimal)
```

## Alternates

Pre-encoded messages (no Ash at the call site):

```elixir
messages = AshA2ui.Info.build_surface(Demo.Minimal)
KinoAsh.Surface.new(messages)
```

A builder MFA:

```elixir
KinoAsh.Surface.new({AshA2ui.Info, :build_surface, [Demo.Minimal]})
```
